[Event "01 - The Orangutan's Core Bargain"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ew6wrQsz9BQ&t=51s"]
[Date "2026.01.??"]
[Round "1"]
[White "Aman Hambleton repertoire"]
[Black "1...e5"]
[Result "*"]

1. b4 e5 2. Bb2 {Do not defend b4 automatically. White attacks Black's central pawn and welcomes Bxb4 Bxe5.} 2... Bxb4 3. Bxe5 Nf6 4. Nf3 O-O 5. e3 {The opening bargain is complete: Black has the extra wing pawn, White the extra central pawn. Develop before trying to prove more.} *

[Event "02 - Nc6: Gain Space with b5"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ew6wrQsz9BQ&t=72s"]
[Date "2026.01.??"]
[Round "2"]
[White "Aman Hambleton repertoire"]
[Black "Nc6 defence"]
[Result "*"]

1. b4 e5 2. Bb2 Nc6 3. b5 {The pawn gains a tempo because the knight must choose a new square. White is not pushing merely to save b4.} 3... Nce7 4. Bxe5 d6 5. Bb2 {Take e5 when it is loose, then preserve the bishop and develop.} *

[Event "03 - The Nb4 Motif"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7xc8814alwM&t=236s"]
[Date "2026.01.??"]
[Round "3"]
[White "Aman Hambleton repertoire"]
[Black "Nb4 knight motif"]
[Result "*"]

1. b4 d5 2. Bb2 Nc6 3. b5 Nb4 4. a3 {A3 questions the knight, but does not trap it automatically. Here d5, d3, c6, and a6 remain legal. Use the trap motif only when the concrete position has removed the retreat squares.} 4... Nxc2+ 5. Qxc2 {In the supplied game Black chose c2 and gave up the knight for a pawn. That was a practical mistake, not a forced consequence of Nb4.} *

[Event "04 - Meet Nd4 with e3"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ew6wrQsz9BQ&t=273s"]
[Date "2026.01.??"]
[Round "4"]
[White "Aman Hambleton repertoire"]
[Black "Nd4 retreat"]
[Result "*"]

1. b4 e5 2. Bb2 Nc6 3. b5 Nd4 4. e3 {This attacks the knight, opens the f1-bishop, and keeps pressure on e5.} 4... Nxb5 5. Bxb5 {White exchanges the wing pawn for Black's developed knight.} 5... c6 6. Be2 d6 7. Nf3 *

[Event "05 - Black Takes b4"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IpQFpjVfzzM&t=656s"]
[Date "2026.01.??"]
[Round "5"]
[White "Aman Hambleton repertoire"]
[Black "Bxb4 exchange"]
[Result "*"]

1. b4 e5 2. Bb2 Bxb4 3. Bxe5 Nf6 4. Nf3 O-O 5. e3 d5 6. Be2 {Do not strand the bishop on e5 while chasing the rook. The extra central pawn is the durable gain.} 6... Re8 7. O-O *

